course: dictionary
lesson: 50
title: Long, grand words and their clues
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Some words are long and grand, and they sound old-fashioned. Accoutrement is one of them. You can work it out from the words around it. In «The Rat went on: Here's-a-belt-for-the-Rat, here's-a-belt-for-the-Mole, with every fresh accoutrement», the Rat is getting new belts and pieces of gear, so an accoutrement must be a piece of equipment.
explain: Notice the word's job. It is a noun, and it is usually used in the plural, accoutrements. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? If the Rat is collecting things to carry, the word must name those things. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Grand words often sound a little funny, and writers use them on purpose. Toad's motoring outfits and caravan come with lots of accoutrements, and the big word makes his fuss over his gear sound comic. In everyday talk, «all the accoutrements» just means all the bits and pieces you need for a job or an activity.
fact: Accoutrement is a noun, and it usually appears as accoutrements.
fact: «Accoutrements» means the extra things, clothes or equipment you have or carry for a particular activity or job.
fact: «Accoutrements» can also mean the things that usually go with something, such as the accoutrements of wealth.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the Rat speaks of «every fresh accoutrement», which means every new piece of equipment.
fact: Accoutrement is a formal word, and it can sound funny when used about ordinary things.
exercise: The Rat has «every fresh accoutrement» in the story. What does accoutrement mean here? | *A piece of equipment | A kind of song | A small animal | A river bank
exercise: Mum says, «We need all the accoutrements for the camping trip.» What does all the accoutrements mean? | Nothing at all, because we are not going | Only the food | Just the tent | *All the bits and pieces and gear
exercise: Why does the author use a grand word like accoutrement in a funny story? | It is a colour | It means very cold | *It is a formal word that makes the fuss over gear sound comic | It is a verb meaning to run fast
test: Toad's caravan comes with many accoutrements. What does this suggest? | A caravan with no wheels | A quiet, empty house | Lots of animals living inside | *Lots of extra equipment and gear
test: What can «the accoutrements of wealth» mean? | Poor clothes and bare feet | *The things that usually go with being rich | Old, broken furniture | Money kept safely in a bank
exam: Which sentence uses accoutrement correctly? | Accoutrement is a yellow fruit that grows on trees. | The sky was accoutrement and blue. | He accoutrement ran to the shop. | *The hiker checked her accoutrements: a map, a torch and a flask.
